    "long_instructions": "## Investigate & Modify\r\n\r\nThis is your badge. Update it with your own information, then add something new.\r\n\r\nDo This:\r\n1. Update `name`, `grade`, and `lucky_number` to your own information.\r\n2. Add an `input()` so the program asks for your name instead of it being set directly in the code.\r\n3. Add a new variable called `favorite_color` and give it a value.\r\n4. Add a variable called `is_new_member` and set it to `True` or `False`.\r\n5. Add a new variable that uses math to create a value from one you already have (for example, your lucky number doubled).\r\n6. Use the AI Tutor to help you add your `favorite_color` to the badge visual.\r\n\r\n::: details [Need help?]\r\nAsk the AI Tutor to explain what it changed before you run the program. Check that the new line actually uses your `favorite_color` variable, not a color you didn't ask for.\r\n:::",
